ENTRY            32945   20260728   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        32945001   20260728   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 12         51
TITLE      Cross section measurement for the 232Th(n,f)
            reaction in the 4.50-5.40 MeV region using a time
            projection chamber
AUTHOR     (Haofan Bai, Han Yi, Yankun Sun, Yiwei Hu, Jie Liu,
            Zepeng Wu, Cong Xia, Wenkai Ren, Wentian Cao,
            Tieshuan Fan, Guohui Zhang, Ruirui Fan, Yang Li,
            Wei Jiang, Yonghao Chen, You Lv, Changjun Ning,
            Weihua Jia, Zhiyong Zhang, Haolei Chen, Zhen Chen,
            Maoyuan Zhao, Changqing Feng, Shubin Liu)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRBJG,3CPRIHP,3CPRNIX,3CPRHST)
           (3CPRCPR) Spallation Neutron Source Science Center,
            Dongguan; Xian Jiaotong University, Xian.
REFERENCE  (J,CPH/C,48,104001,2024)
           #doi:10.1088/1674-1137/ad5ae6
FACILITY   (VDG,3CPRBJG) 4.5 MV Van de Graaff accelerator
INC-SOURCE (D-D) Quasi-monoenergetic neutrons were produced
            through the 2H(d,n) 3He reaction using the deuterium
            gas target. The deuteron beam current was
            approximately 0.5-0.8 uA, and neutrons were obtained
            in the 0 degree direction with respect to the
            deuteron beam line. The deuterium gas target was 2.0
            cm in length with a 5-um-thick molybdenum film, and
            the gas pressure was 3.0 atm.
SAMPLE     A 232Th(OH)4 sample was mounted on the cathodes of
            the TPC with isotopic enrichment of 100%, diameter of
            44.0 mm, thickness of 601.9 ug/cm2, number of nuclei
            of 1.808E19.
DETECTOR   (TPC) The time projection chamber was used as the
            fission fragments and alpha particles detector.
           (FISCH,SCIN) A small fission chamber with a 238U3O8
            sample was used to determine the neutron flux. An
            EJ-309 scintillator detector was used to determine
            the neutron energy spectra.
MONITOR   2(92-U-238(N,F),,SIG))
MONIT-REF 2(,,3,ENDF/B-VIII.0,9237,2018)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) The total uncertainty, 4.1%-4.7%
           (ERR-1) The numbers of 238U nuclei
           (ERR-2) The numbers of 232Th nuclei
           (ERR-3) The net fission counts of the 232Th(n,f)
           (ERR-4) The net fission counts of the 238U(n,f)
           (ERR-5) The detection efficiency of the small fission
                   chamber
           (ERR-6) The detection efficiency of TPC
           (ERR-7) The correction coefficient of the low-energy
                   neutrons
           (ERR-8) The ratio of the main neutron flux through
                   the 238U3O8 sample to that through the
                   232Th(OH)4 sample
HISTORY    (20260728C) Jimin WANG
           (20260731R) The ratio and standard cross section
            received from Haofan Bai
ENDBIB              51
COMMON               3          3
ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-5
PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT
        1.0        1.5        0.3
ENDCOMMON            3
